-- defect: wrong-arity application — `String.fromInt` (Int -> String) applied to
--         TWO arguments. Applying the `String` result to a further argument
--         unifies `String` with `(Int -> _)`, a clash. This is the over-application
--         shape of the arity defect (distinct from calling a non-function value in
--         `arity_call_value_with_unit.sky`), and it too slipped the shipped CLI
--         because the build driver never ran the checker.
-- rust: reject [E2007] — Rust emits a dedicated arity diagnostic where the
--   oracle emits a generic unify clash; the oracle line below stays true and
--   the two coexisting IS the record of that divergence.
-- oracle: reject [E2001] arity / type mismatch
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)

main =
    println (String.fromInt 1 2)
